※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4528

※ A parameter takes one argument.  It is given twice where a name repeats one
※ an earlier argument already filled -- by its place, as here, or by its own
※ name -- and which of the two was meant is not something to guess at.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u8 = plus(1u8, .n ← 2u8)
    0u6

fn plus(n: u8 ← 1u8) → u8:
    n
